Q okay we will be given an array where we need to find a subarray giving us the the maximum product
the catch here is even we encounter 0's or negitives
when we encounter 0 we just need to see the prefix(left) and suffix(right) of the 0 and then return its max
if we encounter even number of negitives it wont be an issue and we can return the whole string
when we encounter odd number of negitives then we need to do the same thing what we did with 0's
so we will start with the loop from 0 to n-1 where prefix starts multiplying from the start i.e prefix = prefix * nums[i]
and suffix starts multiplying from the last suffix = suffix * nums[n-i-1]
in the end we would have defined ans = -1e9
and we would use 
if(max(prefix,suffix)>ans) then ans = max(ans, max(prefix,suffix))


